    "heading": "Armor Class",
    "lineStart": 12857,
    "lineEnd": 12861
  },
  "section": "8.12",
  "rulesText": "An Armor Class (AC) is the target number for an attack roll. AC represents how difficult it is to hit a target.\n\nYour base AC calculation is 10 plus your Dexterity modifier. If a rule gives you another base AC calculation, you choose which calculation to use; you can't use more than one. See also \"Attack Roll.\""
}
